## 1. Select a room and its participants

Read `GET /v1/conversation/catalog` with your server key, assignment and end-user headers. Use the returned room, persona and coaching-lens IDs. Room-specific participant limits, offered modes and actual user consent apply.

Send this body to `POST /v1/conversation/sessions`. Empty setup is free. Save the returned session ID and keep the same operation ID for an exact retry.

```json
{
  "setup": {
    "kind": "room",
    "room_id": "S01",
    "mode": "guided",
    "participants": [
      {
        "persona_id": "jon_guarded_report"
      }
    ]
  },
  "controls": {
    "cast_language": "en-US",
    "cast_speech": "natural"
  }
}
```

For open practice, use `kind: "open"`, `mode: "open_practice"`, a supported participant list and `cast_shape: "one_on_one"` or `"room"`. An optional topic is limited to 240 characters.

```ts
// Run on your server. Keep the key out of browser code and logs.
const base = process.env.FOREVERLEARNING_BASE_URL; // assigned HTTPS /v1 host
const headers = {
  Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.FOREVERLEARNING_API_KEY,
  'X-Assignment-Id': process.env.FOREVERLEARNING_ASSIGNMENT_ID,
  'X-User-Id': 'pseudonymous-learner-42',
  'Content-Type': 'application/json',
  'Idempotency-Key': savedSetupOperationId,
};
const response = await fetch(base + '/conversation/sessions', {
  method: 'POST', headers, body: JSON.stringify(setup), redirect: 'error',
});
if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Setup failed: ' + response.status);
const session = await response.json(); // persist session.session_id
// For POST /chat, use a NEW saved operation ID and read text/event-stream.
// On an uncertain outcome, retry the ORIGINAL body with its ORIGINAL ID.
```

A room’s handling comes from its authored tier, listed in the catalog as `tiers` and `default_tier`. For a gentler start, choose a gentle room or open practice with `high_care: true`; room setups refuse `high_care`. During a session, the learner’s `soften` consent choice switches any room to gentle handling. Consent is one decision per session: repeating the same decision returns the saved result, and a different second decision returns `409`. An empty `consent` object grants nothing.

## 2. Open the room and continue

Send the opening to `POST /v1/chat` with a new saved idempotency key. An opening is a billable generated turn; it has no learner message. Send it before the learner’s first turn and let it finish: a learner turn on a conversation whose opening has not been sent is refused with `409 CONVERSATION_OPENING_REQUIRED`, and one sent while the opening is still running with `409 REQUEST_IN_PROGRESS`.

```json
{
  "session_id": "SAVED_SESSION_ID",
  "conversation": {
    "operation": "opening"
  }
}
```

Continue on the same session with the learner’s words. Five controls can change: cast language, speech style, challenge, emotional heat and coaching lens. Omitted controls keep their last saved value. Coach’s ordinary language is English. Cast language codes are `en-US`, `es-US`, `fr-FR`, `fr-CA`, `de-DE`, `it-IT`, `pt-BR`, `ja-JP`, `ko-KR` and `cmn-CN`.

```json
{
  "session_id": "SAVED_SESSION_ID",
  "prompt": "What would help us agree on the next step?",
  "conversation": {
    "operation": "turn",
    "controls": {
      "challenge": "supportive"
    }
  }
}
```

Parse server-sent events. Content is provisional until the saved `conversation_turn` event; `done` supplies its text/audio receipt. Display safety status separately. A disconnect or error does not prove that a charge was refunded.

Emotional heat is `calm`, `tense` or `heated` when you prepare a room. `raw`, with no filter, is chosen inside the conversation, on the opening or any turn. Characters say exactly what they think, harshly and in character, and may walk out; the safety limits still apply. Offer `raw` only as your user’s own choice.

Retry the exact request with its original idempotency key, or use `GET /v1/requests/REQUEST_ID` to check it; a lookup that finds no request of this learner with that ID answers `404 DEVELOPER_REQUEST_NOT_FOUND`. Do not submit a fresh purchase while the earlier outcome is uncertain. Reusing a key with a different body returns `422`. A turn that failed and was not charged is final for its key: the same key returns `409 REQUEST_FAILED`, so send it again with a new key. If an opening fails, its conversation closes without charge; create a new session. If a generated reply fails validation before anything is shown, the service regenerates it once; that turn takes longer and is still charged once.

Close with `POST /v1/sessions/SESSION_ID/end` and a saved UUID `operation_id`. The generated closeout bills when committed. A room may also end naturally.

A learner has one active session at a time. Opening the learner’s next session closes the open one with a closeout, charged as a closeout ($0.03), the same as ending it yourself. Preparing a session closes nothing. Ending is optional: call `POST /v1/sessions/SESSION_ID/end` when you want the debrief right away.

